To make the circle element in this CSS code look more 3D, you can try adding some perspective and depth to its appearance using the following modifications:

1. Add perspective to the container element (`#chart-area`) to create a 3D effect:

```css
#chart-area {
  ...
  perspective: 1000px;
}
```

2. Rotate the circle element on the Z axis to give it a 3D rotation:

```css
.circle {
  ...
  transform: rotateZ(20deg) translateZ(-100px);
}
```

Here, we're rotating the circle by 20 degrees around the Z axis and moving it back by -100 pixels along the Z axis to give it a sense of depth.

3. Increase the size of the circle to make it more prominent in the 3D space:

```css
.circle {
  ...
  width: 100px; /* increase the diameter */
  height: 100px;
}
```

These modifications will make the circle appear more 3D and add depth to your design. You may need to adjust the values to suit your specific needs and preferences. Remember to test your changes in a browser with WebGL support for optimal results.

