```css
#chart-area {
  perspective: 1000px;
}
```

2. Add a `transform` property with a `translateZ` value to move the circle forward and backward in the 3D space. A negative value will move it back and a positive value will bring it forward. You can also use the `rotateX`, `rotateY`, or `rotateZ` properties to rotate the circle along its respective axis.

```css
.circle {
  transform: translateZ(-20px) scale(1.2);
  /* Rotation examples */
  /* transform: rotateX(20deg) rotateY(30deg); */
  /* transform: rotateZ(10deg); */
}
```

3. Adjust the `box-shadow` property to add depth to the circle by using multiple shadows with different blur radii and colors. This creates a sense of light and shadow on the edges of the circle.

```css
.circle {
  box-shadow: 10px 10px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6), -10px -10px 20px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
