To divide an hour into 10 equal parts, you need to find the duration of each part (i.e., the width of each bin). Since there are 60 minutes in an hour, and we want to divide it into 10 equal parts, the width of each bin is:

bin_width = 60 minutes / 10 bins = 6 minutes

Now that you know the bin width, you can calculate the start and end times of each bin. The start time of the first bin is 0 minutes, and the end time is 6 minutes. The start time of the second bin is 6 minutes, and the end time is 12 minutes, and so on. Here's a formula that calculates the start and end times of the kth bin:

start_time[k] = (k - 1) * bin_width
end_time[k] = start_time[k] + bin_width

