```scala
// Code to handle user input and extract entities
val userInput = "I'm interested in buying a smartwatch with GPS and heart rate monitoring. What do you recommend?"
val features = extractFeatures(userInput)

// Code to manage conversation flow
val intent = getIntent(userInput)
if (intent == RECOMMEND_PRODUCT) {
  if (features.isEmpty) {
    // Code to handle error
    respond("I'm sorry, I didn't catch the features you're looking for. Could you please try again?")
  } else {
    // Code to generate recommendation
    val recommendedProducts = findRecommendedProducts(features)
    if (recommendedProducts.isEmpty) {
      respond("I'm sorry, we don't have any products that meet your requirements at this time.")
    } else {
      val recommendedProduct = selectRecommendedProduct(recommendedProducts)
      respond(s"Based on your preferences, I recommend the ${recommendedProduct.name}. You can learn more about it at ${recommendedProduct.url}.")
    }
  }
} else {
  // Code to handle other intents
  // ...
}
```

This code handles a user's request for product recommendations by extracting the desired features from their message, and then using a state machine to manage the conversation flow. Based on the user's feature preferences, the chatbot recommends a specific product and provides a link for further information. If no products match the user's requirements, the chatbot informs the user accordingly.

