To run the sandbox version of U-Boot, you need to follow these general steps:

1. Obtain the sandboxed version of U-Boot. This can be downloaded from the official U-Boot Git repository by checking out the `u-boot-sandbox` branch or tag.

2. Build and configure U-Boot for your specific target hardware. This involves running the U-Boot build script with appropriate configuration options.

3. Enable the sandboxing feature in U-Boot. This is done by adding the following line to your board's device tree file:

```
&sci {
   compatible = "arm,cortex-a9-sci";
   reg = <0x4000000 0x1000>;
   sci@0 {
      #address-cells = <2>;
      #size-cells = <2>;
      sbi-version = <3>;
      reset-reason = <&reset>;
      sbi {
         compatible = "arm,sbi";
         #system-clock-frequency = <26000000>;
         sgdb = <0>;
         debug-uart = <0>;
         nmi-watchdog = <1>;
         trusted-firmware = <1>;
         trusted-firmware-id = "U-Boot SBI Sandbox";
         sec_init_r = <&sec>;
         sec_init_w = <&sec>;
         sec_init_x = <&sec>;
         pmu_ctrl = <&pmu>;
         pmu_status = <&pmu>;
         pmu_config = <&pmu>;
         pmu_lock = <&pmu>;
         pmu_unlock = <&pmu>;
         pmu_debug = <&pmu>;
         sci_lock = <&sci>;
