Here's an example of how you can create a socket for a chatroom using PHP and Socket.IO:

First, make sure you have installed the necessary packages:

```bash
composer require socketio/socket.io-client
```

Then, create a new PHP file (e.g., `chatroom.php`) and add the following code:

```php
<?php
require_once 'db_connect.php'; // replace this with your database connection script
require_once 'socket.io-client.js';

// define the URL to connect to
$socketUrl = "http://localhost:3000";

// authenticate user and get session ID
$userId = "your_user_id";
$sessionId = getSessionId($userId);

// initialize socket.io client
$socket = io($socketUrl);

// join chatroom with given ID
$chatroomId = "your_chatroom_id";
$socket->emit("joinRoom", [$sessionId, $chatroomId]);

// listen for messages sent in chatroom
$socket->on("message", function ($data) {
    // process message data here
});

function getSessionId($userId)
{
    global $conn;

    // query database to retrieve session ID for given user
    $stmt = $conn->prepare("SELECT session_id FROM sessions WHERE user_id = ?");
    $stmt->bind_param("s", $userId);
    $stmt->execute();
    $result = $stmt->get_result();
    $sessionId = "";
    if ($result->num_rows > 0) {
        $row = $result->fetch_assoc();
        $sessionId = $row["session_id"];
    }
    return $sessionId;
}
```

