To push the `mnpStatus` retrieved from the API into the corresponding registration object in your `registrations` state, you can modify your `checkMNPStatusAPI` function as follows:

```jsx
checkMNPStatusAPI(phoneNo, index) {
  console.log("mnpphoneno: " + phoneNo);

  const headers = new Headers();
  headers.append("Authorization", "Bearer " + user.getAccessToken());

  fetch(api.checkPortInStatus(user.getProductCode(), phoneNo), {
    headers: headers,
    method: "GET"
  })
    .then(r => r.json())
    .then(rJson => {
      const updatedRegistrations = [...this.state.registrations]; // Create a copy of the current state
